    <h1>Trust &amp; Safety</h1>
    <p>Nyumba254 is Kenya’s open platform to list, find and manage property. Every listing shows who listed it and what a viewing costs, before you get in touch.</p>
    <p class="draft-note"><strong>Draft, needs legal review.</strong> This page explains our approach in plain language. It is not a legal agreement and may change.</p>

    <h2>Roles and verification</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A role is a claim.</strong>Each account says whether it is an owner, caretaker, agent or company. This is self-declared when the account is created.</li>
      <li><strong>Verification is proof.</strong>A role badge appears only after Nyumba254 has checked the supporting documents for that role. Listers without verification show “(not verified)”. An identity check confirms who the account holder is; it does not guarantee a property or a transaction.</li>
      <li><strong>Social links are self-declared.</strong>Links a lister adds to their Lister Page are not verified by Nyumba254.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Viewing fees</h2>
    <p>Where an agent or company charges for a viewing, the fee is shown on the listing before you make contact. You pay only that fee, at the property, to the person you meet, and you ask for a receipt. Read the full <a href="/viewing-fee-policy">Viewing Fee Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Common scams in Kenya and what to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A “caretaker” asks for a deposit before you view.</strong>Never pay rent or a deposit before you have seen the property in person and met the person you are paying.</li>
      <li><strong>“Booking” or “reservation” fees.</strong>The only fee a lister may ask for is the disclosed viewing fee, paid at the property. Other pre-contract charges are against our policy.</li>
      <li><strong>M-Pesa “reversal” requests.</strong>If someone says they sent money by mistake and asks you to send it back, do not reply with money. Check your M-Pesa message and contact Safaricom.</li>
      <li><strong>Photos copied from other listings.</strong>If photos look too good, or the lister cannot show you the actual unit, treat it as a warning sign.</li>
      <li><strong>Urgency and pressure.</strong>“Many people are coming today” is a common push to pay fast. A genuine lister will let you view first.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment requests through social media or direct messages.</strong>Pay viewing fees only at the property, never through direct messages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to report</h2>
    <p>Use the report option on any listing or Lister Page, or <a href="/contact">contact us</a>. Include the listing, what was asked for, and any screenshots or receipts. Do not delete messages.</p>

    <h2>What Nyumba254 will and will not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We will</strong>review reports, hide listings or social links that break the rules, and suspend accounts for serious or repeated breaches.</li>
      <li><strong>We will not</strong>collect or hold viewing fees, rent or deposits, mediate payments or refunds, or take a commission from your agreement.</li>
    </ul>
